  "S3": {
   "id": "S3",
   "kind": "document",
   "title": "Ml Model Diagnostics Handbook",
   "text": "2. Variance in Machine Learning\nIn machine learning the variance of a model is how much its predictions change when it is trained\non different training sets drawn from the same source. High-variance models such as deep\ndecision trees fit the quirks of one training set. This is a property of the learning algorithm, not the\nspread of a data column.\nThe spread of a feature column is a different matter. In scikit-learn VarianceThreshold removes\nfeatures whose variance is below a threshold; the default threshold is 0.0, which removes only\nconstant features.",
   "doc_id": "ml_model_diagnostics_handbook",
   "course_id": "ml",
   "location": "p.2",
   "chunk_id": "ml_model_diagnostics_handbook:0001",
   "score": 0.3824,
   "data": {
